      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This chapter looks at therapies that are considered \"alternative\" to conventional medical approaches. A definition of \"complementary and alternative\" medicine is considered in the context of the complex and clinically challenging field of pain medicine. A rationale for studying unorthodox treatments of chronic pain is presented. The challenges of an evidence-based approach to incorporating complementary therapies are explored, and a brief survey of several commonly available complementary medicine therapies is provided."},
